# Plan D on UHeM: a reproduction and a longer schedule of the same recipe.
#
# Source: the Plan D run of 2026-09-20 (suite moon_deg25to200_alt100to1000km_20260704_103234,
# 512x5 residual SIREN, potential_autograd residual SH25 -> SH200, 1,848,321 parameters,
# best epoch 792 of 800). The flags are its recorded command line (command.txt,
# sha256 be488c527336ba2cbd2b40aa731e79f1ac59c973e4bfc23fe0ce085dc0668f9f) with
# repeated flags resolved the argparse way (the later value wins: --epochs 800,
# --t-max 780, --min-lr-ratio 0.01, --patience 150, --direction-loss-floor-abs 1e-7)
# and the data and output paths removed (the launcher and the submit line supply
# them). Resolved with the trainer parser of 2026-10-23, line 0 matches the run's
# config.json in 146 of 152 TrainConfig fields; the other 6 (degree_min/max,
# w0_bands, x_scale_m, resolved_r_ref_m, output_envelope_power) are filled in from
# the dataset at run time. The training code itself has changed since that run, so
# line 0 tests whether the recipe still gives the same model, not bit equality.
#
#   0  PlanD_Reproduction_800ep  - the recipe as it ran: 800 epochs, cosine t_max 780
#   1  PlanD_Long_1000ep_tmax980 - the same recipe with the cosine stretched to
#                                  1000 epochs (t_max 980; same 20-epoch tail as line 0)
#
# Both lines share seed 42 and split seed 42, so their val/test splits are the same.
# Walltime: Plan D's 800 epochs took 43.4 h of epoch time on a GTX 1660 Ti (median
# 195 s/epoch, history.csv), so line 1 needs about 54 h at that speed; 4 days
# leaves room for the evaluations. a100q allows 10 days (UHeM wiki, Altay page).
# Submit both at once (one A100 each), from the repo root on the login node:
#
#   set -a; . hpc/cluster.env; set +a
#   SUITE="$LUNARIS_DATA_DIR/datasets/cloud_suites/moon_deg25to200_alt100to1000km_20260704_103234"
#   hpc/submit.sh scenario --array=0-1 --time=4-00:00:00 -- \
#     hpc/scenarios/st_lrps_planD_reproduction_and_long.jsonl \
#     --train-data "$SUITE/train_hybrid_10M.h5" \
#     --val-data   "$SUITE/val_uniform_2M.h5" \
#     --test-data  "$SUITE/test_uniform_2M.h5" \
#     --ood-data   "$SUITE/ood_combined_1000k.h5" \
#     --suite-manifest "$SUITE/manifest.json"
#
# Continue after a walltime stop: the same command with --resume right after the
# JSONL path.
